.)"], "timestamp": "2026-11-21T14:00:20.937Z", "title": "The Austin weekly statesman", "type": ["title"], "url": "https://www.loc.gov/item/sn86088296/"}, {"access_restricted": false, "aka": ["http://www.loc.gov/item/sn83021327/", "http://lccn.loc.gov/sn83021327", "https://search.catalog.loc.gov/instances/31e3c172-4dca-5406-8235-0e3f1327d72e"], "batch": ["txdn_audi_ver01"], "campaigns": [], "date": "1871", "description": ["Weekly Vol. 1, no. 1 (Aug. 1, 1871)-v. 12, no. 42 (June 28, 1883). Archived issues are available in digital format as part of the Library of Congress Chronicling America online collection. Daily edition: Democratic statesman (Austin, Tex. : 1871), 1871-187u; Daily democratic statesman (Austin, Tex. : 1873), 1873-1880; Austin daily statesman (Austin, Tex. : 1880), 1880-1883. Austin weekly statesman 2331-6519 (DLC)sn 86088296 (OCoLC)13958767"], "digitized": true, "extract_timestamp": "2026-11-19T16:26:38.032Z", "group": ["newspaper-titles", "ndnp/newspapers", "catalog-split-11", "catalog", "united-states-newspaper-directory", "main-catalog-split-11"], "hassegments": false, "id": "http://www.loc.gov/item/sn83021327/", "image_url": [], "index": 6, "language": ["english"], "latlong": [30.264979, -97.746598], "location": ["travis", "texas", "austin", "united states"], "location_str": "", "lonlat": [-97.746598, 30.264979], "number": ["10125278", "http://www.loc.gov/item/sn83021327/1871-08-01/ed-1/", "online resource", "american antiquarian soc, newsp proj", "microfilm master", "2026-04-13t21:30:13", "sn83021326", "466", "http://www.loc.gov/item/sn83021327/1883-04-12/ed-1/", "1", "panhandle-plains hist mus", "microfilm service copy", "monmouth col", "sn86088147", "original", "2026-08-05t10:51:28", "2025-05-09t12:48:08.015499", "sn83021327", "sn86088296", "sn86088324", "univ of texas at austin", "texas state libr", "2331-3242"], "original_format": ["newspaper"], "other_title": ["Weekly statesman"], "partof": ["serial and government publications division", "catalog", "the weekly democratic statesman (austin, tex.) 1871-1883", "directory of u.s. newspapers in american libraries", "chronicling america"], "publication_frequency": ["weekly"], "score": 20.714184, "shelf_id": "Newspaper", "site": ["chroniclingamerica", "usnd", "catalog"], "subject": ["united states", "newspapers", "texas", "austin", "travis", "austin (tex.)"], "timestamp": "2026-11-21T13:30:08.130Z", "title": "The weekly democratic statesman", "type": ["title"], "url": "https://www.loc.gov/item/sn83021327/"}], "reproductions": "<p>\nSome images in this collection are described in groups; others are \ndescribed individually. In some cases, all of the images in the \ngroup display online, in other cases they do not.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nYou can download online images yourself.  Alternatively, you can \npurchase copies of various types.\n</p>\n\n<ol>\n<p>\t\n<strong><li>Determine whether the desired materials can be retrieved \nonline.</strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<p>\t\n<li>Look in the <strong>Medium</strong> field above to determine whether\n the description is for one photograph or more than one.</li>\n </p>\n <p>\n<li>If the description is for a single item and it is displaying, \nyou can download or purchase a print.  Cite the number that begins \nwith &quot;LC-DIG...&quot; when purchasing copies through Library of \nCongress Duplication Services.\n</p>\n<p>\n<li>If the description is for more than one item and there is \na &quot;Click for more images&quot; icon displaying, select that. \nIndividual images will display; you can download or purchase prints. \nCite the number that begins with &quot;LC-DIG...&quot; when purchasing \ncopies through Library of Congress Duplication Services.\n</p>\n<p>\n<li>If the description is for more than one item and there is no\n &quot;Click for more images&quot; icon displaying, return to the\n  &quot;About this Item&quot; tab and select the &quot;<i>Check for \n  online items from this group</i>&quot; link.  Then select the \n  \"Obtaining Copies\" tab for any retrieved items that are of interest.\n</p>\n</ul>\n</li>\n\n<p>\n<strong><li>If the images do not display online</strong> -- Select images for reproduction through one of these methods:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<p>\t\n<li>Visit the Prints &amp; Photographs Reading Room and request to view \nthe group (general information about service in the reading room is \navailable at: <a href=\"//www.loc.gov/rr/print/info/001_ref.html\">https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/info/001_ref.html</a>).</li>  \n</p>\n<p>\n<li>P&amp;P reading room staff can provide up to 15 photocopies of items \nper calendar year. (Color images cannot be photocopied.) For assistance,\n see our <a href=\"//www.loc.gov/rr/askalib/ask-print.html\">Ask a Librarian</a> page. OR</li>\n</p>\n<p>\n<li>Hire a freelance researcher to do further selection for you \n(a list of researchers is available at: \n<a href=\"//www.loc.gov/rr/print/resource/013_pic.html\">https://www.loc.gov/rr/print/resource/013_pic.html</a>).\n</p>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>\n<strong>Purchasing Copies</strong>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nLibrary of Congress Duplication Services can make copies of various \ntypes from images in Prints & Photographs Division Collections.  \nPrice lists, contact information, and order forms are available on the \n<a href=\"//www.loc.gov/duplicationservices/\">Duplication Services Web site</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nCarol M. Highsmith sells prints of her photographs at: <a href=\"http://photographsamerica.com/\">http://photographsamerica.com/</a> .\n</p>  \n\n\n\n\n        ", "resources": [{"caption": "original digital file", "files": [[{"height": 280, "levels": 1, "mimetype": "image/jpeg", "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:28200:28295/full/pct:6.25/0/default.jpg", "width": 408}, {"height": 561, "levels": 1, "mimetype": "image/jpeg", "url": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:28200:28295/full/pct:12.5/0/default.jpg", "width": 817}, {"height": 1122, "levels": 1, 